    "query": "What are the admission requirements for international students?",
    "response": {
      "answer": "According to the information provided on HTW Berlin's website, the admission requirements for international students are as follows:\n\n* If you have a higher education entrance qualification from abroad, your application will be pre-checked by uni-assist.\n* Please submit all necessary application documents by the following dates:\n\t+ For summer semester: 31 December\n\t+ For winter semester: 30 June\n* uni-assist will assess whether your foreign certificates meet the standards of the Standing Conference of the Ministers of Education and Cultural Affairs (Central Office for Foreign Education / Zentralstelle für ausländisches Bildungswesen – ZaB) and are sufficient for admission to higher education in Germany.\n* If you are unable to provide all of your certificates from your country of origin, uni-assist will forward your application to HTW Berlin after you have proven your refugee status with a copy of your residence permit.\n* HTW Berlin will then decide whether your application can be considered.\n* If the pre-check performed by uni-assist determines that your foreign education certificates do not give you direct entitlement to study at HTW Berlin, you can apply for a preparatory course called a Studienkolleg (indirect entitlement to study).\n\nIt's also important to note that international students may need to provide additional documentation, such as proof of German language proficiency, and may be required to take a language proficiency test (e.g. DSH exam).",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Proof of English proficiency",
          "url": "https://www.htw-berlin.de/en/studies/applications/application-via-uni-assist/proof-of-english-proficiency/",
